  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness based on probability mass on unfavorable outcomes) is not considered by the individual. The individual does not evaluate the distribution of probabilities or the extent to which outcomes are skewed toward zero. Instead, the justification is based solely on the magnitude of the potential gain, ignoring the probability structure. The decision reason requires evaluating the skewness—specifically, whether a greater portion of probability is on unfavorable outcomes—and preferring the more right-skewed lottery. Since the individual does not reference skewness or probability distribution shape, and instead focuses on the maximum prize, the decision reason was not used. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason in their deliberation process.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
