  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on skewness — specifically, the extent to which unfavorable outcomes (losses) dominate in probability. In this case, B has a higher probability of loss (0.2% > 0.1%), so it is more right-skewed. The reason would therefore prefer B. However, the individual's reasoning focuses entirely on the magnitude of the loss (smaller loss in B), not on the probability distribution or skewness. There is no reference to the shape of the distribution, the relative weights of outcomes, or any evaluation of skewness. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason involving skewness. The reasoning is based on a different criterion (loss magnitude), not on skewness. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
